--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LINKING EXCEPTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

As a special exception, the copyright holder gives permission to link this
program with the following proprietary components, and to convey the resulting
executable, provided you otherwise comply with the AGPL for this program's own
code:

  * Google ML Kit (com.google.mlkit:*)
  * Google Play services and Google Mobile Services libraries
    (com.google.android.gms:*)
  * Google AICore and MediaPipe on-device inference runtimes, if and when this
    program uses them

WHY THIS EXISTS. Rekhon reads receipts on the device using Google ML Kit
(issue 3.8, FR-OCR-002). ML Kit is proprietary and cannot be relicensed under the
AGPL, so distributing an APK containing both this program and ML Kit would
otherwise be an unresolvable conflict rather than a licensing choice. This
exception resolves it, and nothing more: it permits linking against the named
components only, and does not weaken any AGPL obligation on Rekhon's own source.

If you modify this program, you may extend this exception to your version, but
you are not obliged to. If you do not wish to, delete this paragraph and the
exception above from your version.

The coupling this exception covers is deliberately narrow and easy to remove:
ML Kit is reachable from exactly one class, MlKitReceiptTextRecognizer, behind
the ReceiptTextRecognizer interface, and no domain model references an ML Kit
type. A fully free build substituting an open-source recogniser is a contained
change, and needs no part of this exception.

